  "limitations": [
    "Fidelity import reconstructs completed long positions; short sales and position flips remain unsupported",
    "Ambiguous Fidelity quantity units are reconciled against recorded exits and explicitly marked for review when the mismatch exceeds tolerance",
    "No direct Fidelity API, credential access, position sync, or order placement",
    "No options calculations",
    "Screenshot attachments are stored in the portable data directory and should be kept small",
    "Microsoft WebView2 must be available on the Windows computer",
    "Generated journal insights are descriptive rules, not predictions or personalized financial advice",
    "Practice completion is not retained-mastery certification",
    "Back-tests use bar-level OHLCV approximations and cannot determine intrabar event order",
    "Paper trading uses locally stored historical bars and does not connect to a brokerage or place live orders",
    "If a paper-trade stop and target occur inside the same bar, the simulation conservatively processes the stop first",
    "Paper fills do not model queue position, partial fills, changing spreads, liquidity, market impact, or short availability",
    "The first simulation strategy is a moving-average crossover; it is educational evidence, not a forecast",
    "No execution-quality live market-data feed is included",
    "Massive free one-minute history is end-of-day; Alpaca Basic uses IEX and excludes the latest 15 minutes from REST history",
    "Tradier chart downloads require an eligible brokerage account and token; Alpha Vantage one-minute access is premium",
    "Provider availability, symbol coverage, quotas, retention, and freshness remain controlled by each provider",
    "Fidelity Trader+ has no documented direct chart API; Active Trader Pro Classic chart CSV remains a manual import path",
    "Chart comparisons include only bars with exactly matching timestamps and are normalized to percent change from the first shared visible bar",
    "Regular-session filtering uses New York clock time and the timestamps supplied by the imported or downloaded dataset"
  ]
